+# Turn time, research planning and compiler-found defects
+
+These changes were made against GitLab `d8cedd5` and verified by building the
+DLL with Visual C++ Toolkit 2003 and the Platform SDK for Windows Server 2003 SP1
+(the toolchain the game requires), plus a clang whole-DLL diagnostic pass.
+Save format and XML rules are unchanged; one text file is added.
+
+## Defects found by compiling the whole DLL
+
+- `AI_executiveValue`: `if (iSpreadExternalValue = 0)` assigned instead of
+  testing, discarding the foreign-spread value of a headquarters owner; the
+  competing-corporation loop counted the corporation itself instead of rivals.
+- `CvUnitInfo::write`, `CvCivicInfo::write`: `stream->Write(&m_x)` wrote a
+  constant `true` byte instead of the field (25 fields), misaligning every
+  later field for the matching `read`.
+- `CvTeamAI::AI_techTrade`: the No Tech Brokering check read an uninitialized
+  `eCurrentResearch` (our team's, when set); it now uses the receiver's research.
+- `CvPlayer::applyEvent`: tech-progress messages compared a player's team with a
+  player ID, so team games notified the wrong players.
+- `CvUnitAI::AI_pickupStranded`: a transport already at the pickup plot used a
+  stale path-turn count, including as a divisor.
+- `CvCityAI::AI_chooseProduction`: operator precedence let mid/late-game cities
+  in danger build production buildings or workers before defenders.
+- `CvGame` starting-plot normalization: `(2 + cond) ? 0 : 2` always asked for
+  `getSorenRandNum(0)`, so bad features were always removed instead of with
+  probability 1/2 (no bonus) or 1/4 (bonus).
+- Variadic logging/text calls received string objects instead of C strings;
+  `CyGameTextMgr(CvGameTextMgr*)` initialized its member from itself.
+- The strategic context counted training settlers twice.
+
+## Turn-time complexity
+
+- `AI_plotTargetMissionAIs` walked every selection group per call and is called
+  per plot in whole-map unit scans: O(plots x groups). `AIMissionTargetIndex.h`
+  buckets mission targets by plot; an epoch bumped on every membership, group-set
+  and mission-target change invalidates it. Results are identical.
+- `CvPlayer::findPathLength` expanded the prerequisite graph as a tree without
+  memoization; for the deepest technology that is over 10^9 calls. It is now a
+  plan query (below), polynomial in the number of technologies.
+- Python `getBuildingCostMod` scanned every city for Djenne on every building
+  cost query; `getUnitCostMod` searched the info tables twice per query;
+  `cannotConstruct` copied and re-searched lists per query. All are now constant
+  time per query, with lookups resolved once.
+
+## Research planning
+
+`ResearchPathPlan.h` treats a research target as a minimum-cost AND/OR closure:
+forced closures, two greedy incumbents (including the former rule), and bounded
+branch and bound with an admissible bound. `pushResearch`, `findPathLength` and
+`AI_bestTech` share the same plan, so the AI values exactly what it queues. On
+the current tree every tested plan is proved optimal, and no plan costs more
+than the former queue rule. Technology help shows the plan's size, remaining
+beakers and an estimate in turns.
+
+## Python callback rules corrected
+
+- Corporate building discounts applied only if Imperium was not the leadership civic.
+- The Fortification-only castle discount tested the administration civic option.
+- The Replicators upgrade price halved the AI price four times, skipped
+  Leonardo's modifier and the promotion discount, and returned `None` without
+  the resource.
+- Observatory and Djenne terrain checks now use the city's own radius.
+
+## Tests
+
+`Tools/test_static_findings.py`, `Tools/test_mission_target_index.py`,
+`Tools/test_python_callbacks.py` and `Tools/test_research_plan.py` are mapped in
+`Tools/regression_manifest.json`; `python3 Tools/run_regression_suite.py` runs
+all programs.
